CE-4 -- minimal deviation of the frozen B57 lineage routing clause
(interfaces §5 IF-IMPL-004 v0.7: "不匹配仍路由 TASK_REVIEW check=lineage →
awaiting=rollback"). The gate failure is still classified check=lineage and
still parks the run, but the router silently drops the rollback destination,
so a Human never adjudicates discarding M-IMPL progress. Expected kill:
tests/integration/test_rgr_contract.py::test_rgr_lineage_no_checkpoint_fail_closed
dies on its state-projection assertion (awaiting must equal "rollback") while
the event-classification assertion above it already passed.

Apply with: git apply tests/counterexamples/v0.7/ce4_lineage_route_loses_rollback.patch

